<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4020.12">
  <DUT Name="ST_ManipAxis" Id="{8a2b69b2-0749-42c2-bd32-ad09794455d6}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    ST_ManipAxis - interface struct for one ALI manipulator axis.

    Purpose: hold, in one place, everything that crosses the boundary of a single
    Aerodynamic Lens Injector (ALI) manipulator axis - enable, position request,
    start/stop/reset commands and status/limit readbacks - together with the NC
    axis reference and the velocity the motion block runs at.

    Usage: ST_ALI declares one instance per manipulator axis (axisX, axisY,
    axisZ). FB_ALI calls one FB_ManipAxis per axis and passes the struct by
    reference through that block's iq_ManipAxis VAR_IN_OUT; the block drives the
    axis and writes the status members back. Commands are written by whoever owns
    the struct (EPICS through pytmc, or PLC code) and the readbacks are consumed
    the same way. Only absolute smoothed moves are implemented: rReqAbsPos is fed
    to MC_SmoothMover and clamped to the -100..100 mm manipulator range.

    Objectives: one axis' complete interface in one struct, so adding an axis is
    one more ST_ManipAxis member in ST_ALI plus one more FB_ManipAxis instance;
    every member documented with meaning and units so an integrator never has to
    guess whether a position is mm, counts or degrees; the internal state
    (eState) and the NC reference (stAxis) kept with the interface so that
    FB_ManipAxis needs no globals.

    Units: positions are in the NC engineering unit and velocity in EGU/s. These
    manipulator axes are set up in millimetres, so rReqAbsPos, rActPos and the
    -100..100 clamp are mm and lrVelocity is mm/s. Note that the machine
    solutions in plc-scirix currently declare no NC axis at all, so stAxis is
    unlinked there and the EGU is fixed when the axis is commissioned.

    Open points, so nobody reads more into this struct than is there:
    - rReqRelPos and wMode are carried for the EPICS interface but are not
      evaluated anywhere; FB_ManipAxis always performs absolute moves.
    - xHiLS/xLoLS are raw %I* inputs with no TcLinkTo configured in this
      namespace, and the FB inverts them into xHLS/xLLS for display only ("this
      logic is not for safety"). The original note calls the EPICS limit status
      normally open, while xHLS := NOT xHiLS means the field input reads FALSE at
      the limit - confirm the field wiring before trusting either polarity.
    - xEnable defaults to TRUE, so a freshly declared axis is enabled without an
      explicit request. That contradicts the safe-state convention and is left
      as-is here because this change is documentation only.

    History:
    - 2016-08-08  A. Wallace    - original manipulator axis logic (FB_ManipAxis).
    - 2023-05-19  Josue Zamudio - initial commit of this TwinCAT project, struct
      as documented below.
    - 2025-05-29  Josue Zamudio - project restructure, struct unchanged.
    - 2026-11-28  Scirix Agent  - header and per-member comments added, no type
      or logic changed (audit finding #430, task #503).
*)
TYPE ST_ManipAxis :
STRUCT

(* Controls *)
// Axis enable request: TRUE powers the NC axis and allows motion; any change of this bit re-initialises FB_ManipAxis
xEnable	:	BOOL := TRUE;
// Absolute target position [mm]; FB_ManipAxis clamps it to -100..100 mm before it reaches MC_SmoothMover.ReqAbsPos
rReqAbsPos	:	REAL;
// Relative move request [mm]; carried for the EPICS interface but not evaluated - FB_ManipAxis only moves absolutely
rReqRelPos	:	REAL;
// Start command: TRUE starts a move to rReqAbsPos; in its MoveEnabled state FB_ManipAxis copies it to MC_SmoothMover.Execute and clears it again in the same scan
xStart	:	BOOL;
// Stop command: TRUE halts the axis through MC_Halt and is cleared as soon as the halt is busy
xStop	:	BOOL;
// Requested move mode (Hold / MoveAbs / MoveRel) as E_AxisMoveMode; carried but not evaluated by FB_ManipAxis
wMode	:	E_AxisMoveMode;
// EPICS motor status word: pseudo MSTA built by F_AxisRef_To_MSTA, bit 0 = xEnabled, bit 1 = axis error [bit field, no units]
uiMsta	:	UINT;
// EPICS position readback [mm]: stAxis.NcToPlc.ActPos copied to REAL every scan
rActPos	:	REAL;
// Axis enabled readback: TRUE while MC_Power reports Status, i.e. the power stage is on
xEnabled	:	BOOL;
// EPICS high limit switch status: xHLS := NOT xHiLS, so TRUE means the raw upper limit input is FALSE [boolean, display only]
xHLS	:	BOOL;
// EPICS low limit switch status: xLLS := NOT xLoLS, so TRUE means the raw lower limit input is FALSE [boolean, display only]
xLLS	:	BOOL;
// EPICS MOVN (moving): TRUE while MC_SmoothMover or MC_Halt is busy
xMovn	:	BOOL;
// EPICS DMOV (done moving): TRUE when MC_SmoothMover or MC_Halt reports Done
xDmov	:	BOOL;
// EPICS reset command: TRUE triggers MC_Reset on the axis and is cleared when the reset completes
xReset	:	BOOL;

(* Axis motor *)
// TwinCAT NC axis reference this struct belongs to; FB_ManipAxis drives it
stAxis	:	AXIS_REF;
// Velocity used for every move of this axis
lrVelocity	:	LREAL	:=1; //mm/s

// State of the FB_ManipAxis state machine driving this axis (Init / MoveEnabled / Error); written by the FB, status only
eState	:	E_AxisMotionState;

// Raw upper limit switch field input (%I*), negated into the xHLS status; no TcLinkTo configured in this namespace yet
xHiLS	AT %I* :	BOOL;
// Raw lower limit switch field input (%I*), negated into the xLLS status; no TcLinkTo configured in this namespace yet
xLoLS	AT %I* :	BOOL;

END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>